      "year": 2020,
      "abstract": "The Modeling Architectures and Parameterization for Spacecraft (MAPS) environment was created to realize the model-based systems engineering (MBSE) philosophy for spacecraft applications. MAPS combines the Systems Modeling Language (SysML) for initial templates and requirements, system parametric sizing, and optimization in order to model space architectures. Further, it employs system-of-systems engineering practices for architectural analysis (e.g. complexity and flexibility metrics) and also integrates orbital trajectory analysis for mission simulations. The environment has potential to improve efficiency and completeness in studies of spacecraft constellations; on-orbit servicing, assembly, and manufacturing; or other emerging concepts. In addition to detailing the above features, this paper demonstrates the use of MAPS with low-Earth orbit satellite constellation study.",
